---
import MarketingLayout from '~/layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '~/site';

/**
 * DRAFT — not legal advice and not reviewed by a lawyer.
 *
 * What is stated below about *this website* is factually accurate as built:
 * no analytics, no cookies, no third-party requests, no forms posting anywhere.
 * The sections about products describe the intended position and must be
 * checked against what each product actually does before launch.
 *
 * Have this reviewed before simplifybase.com goes live.
 */
const lastUpdated = '5 August 2026';
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What SimplifyBase collects, what it does not, and what happens to it."
>
  <section class="border-b border-line">
    <div class="container-page pt-16 pb-12 sm:pt-20 sm:pb-14">
      <p class="text-eyebrow mb-5">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="text-headline">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-xs text-faint">
        Last updated {lastUpdated}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container-page py-14 sm:py-20">
    <div
      class="mb-10 rounded-xl border border-dashed border-line-strong bg-surface p-5"
    >
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <strong class="text-ink">This is a draft.</strong> It describes the position
        we intend to hold and, for the website itself, the position as built. It
        has not been reviewed by a lawyer and should be before launch.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        simplifybase.com is a static site. It sets no cookies, runs no
        analytics, and makes no requests to third-party servers — fonts and
        scripts are served from this domain. Nothing you do here is tracked
        across sessions or across sites.
      </p>
      <p>
        The one exception is the theme toggle, which stores your light/dark
        preference in your browser's local storage under the key
        <code>sb-theme</code>. That value never leaves your device.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our hosting provider keeps standard server access logs, which include IP
        addresses, for a limited period for security and diagnostic purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>The contact form</h2>
      <p>
        The contact form does not post to a server. Submitting it opens your own
        email client with the fields filled in — nothing is transmitted until
        you press send, and it is sent by you, to us, as an ordinary email.
      </p>
      <p>
        Emails you send us are kept for as long as needed to answer you and to
        keep a record of the conversation. We do not add you to a mailing list
        without asking.
      </p>

      <h2>The products</h2>
      <p>
        Each product documents its own data handling in detail, because they
        differ. The general position across all of them:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Products run against your own database wherever that is possible. On
          self-hosted products, that means your data does not leave your server.
        </li>
        <li>
          Where hosted processing genuinely helps, it is opt-in, scoped to the
          minimum data required, and described in the product's documentation
          rather than only here.
        </li>
        <li>
          Models are per-customer. Your data is never pooled into a shared model
          or used to train anything another customer benefits from.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        For SimplifyStock specifically, see
        <a href="/product/simplifystock/docs/data-and-privacy/"
          >Data and privacy</a
        > — it lists exactly which fields are read, which tables are written, and
        what is transmitted if you enable hosted forecasting.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        If you are in the UK or the EU you have rights of access, correction,
        erasure, restriction, portability and objection over personal data we
        hold about you. Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and
        we will action it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes materially, the date at the top changes and, for
        anything that affects existing customers, we will email you rather than
        rely on you noticing.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about any of this go to
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</MarketingLayout>
